    {
      "caption": "Misconception: a bigger intercept does not mean steeper",
      "duration_ms": 9000,
      "id": "s5",
      "narration": "Which is steeper: A, y equals four x minus six, or B, y equals x plus three? The plus three looks bigger \u2014 but steepness is the gradient, not the intercept. A has gradient four against B's one, so A climbs fastest, even though B crosses the y-axis higher at three. Compare the m, never the c.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at_ms": 0,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "title",
            "kind": "text",
